kthroughs and reference imagery to guide real-time educational scanning; and Butterfly iQ+/iQ3 Vet, a third generation handheld ultrasound system. It sells and markets its products through a direct sales force, distributors, and e-commerce channels. Butterfly Network, Inc. was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph M. DeVivo | CEO, President & Chairman of the Board | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 220 people. Revenue per employee of $444K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $107K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Butterfly Network, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.7B market cap on $98M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -168% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 47%.","The company is burning through $16M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -21.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -58.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 4.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 24% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there 